<a href="/user:info/pedantique" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(0); return false;">
T"pedantique"
</a>
</span>
<br>
T" "
<strong>
T"Author Page:"
</strong>
T" "
<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/pedantique-personnel-file">
T"Dr. Dentick's Personnel File"
</a>
</p>
<p>
<strong>
<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/maim-the-sky-slay-the-sun-hub">
T"Heron &amp; Hound Commentary Corner:"
</a>
</strong>
</p>
<blockquote>
<p>
T""A question, Egret.""
</p>
<p>
T""Yeah, Dhole?""
</p>
<p>
T""Do you not worry over the Houndmaster's secrets?""
</p>
<p>
T""Stop calling her that. Anyway, why would I worry about those? The Overseer trusts me.""
</p>
<p>
T""No more than the desert trusts the sun. What value is trust when you do tricks of your own accord? Would she not enlighten you otherwise? Would she not explain instead of demand?""
</p>
<p>
T""Idiot. An overseer's secret isn't something like that. You don't whisper it to your friend to make them giggle. They bunch them up next to their hearts. They lock them there forever. That's what it takes to protect everyone.""
</p>
<p>
T""Distrust by a prettier name.""
</p>
<p>
T""Sure, but that's the world she distrusts. Not me. Never me.""
</p>
<p>
T""And when her secrets are worth more than your blood? When she cannot gird you against the future, or warn you of a fate? A simple exchange, that.""
</p>
<p>
T""Sure, I'll die. I'll die and be even more trustworthy. Graves don't leak."
</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
